Azure Resource Graph is a service that allows organizations to explore and query information about Azure resources at scale. It is particularly useful when administrators need visibility across multiple subscriptions.

Resource Graph can help identify:

* Resource types
* Resource locations
* Resource groups
* Subscription relationships
* Resource configurations
* Tags
* Operating system information
* Resource counts

For example, an administrator managing 50 subscriptions can query which virtual machines exist across the entire environment instead of manually opening each subscription.

A real-life use case is an enterprise performing an infrastructure inventory before a security audit or migration project.

Azure Resource Graph improves large-scale resource discovery and operational visibility.
